  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 759149,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 100 Classic Books: The Man Who Would Be King - Nintendo DS\n\nEmbark on a literary adventure with *The Man Who Would Be King*, part of Nintendo's 100 Classic Books collection for the Nintendo DS. This thrilling novel by Rudyard Kipling, included within the expansive library housed on a single game cartridge, tells the audacious tale of two British adventurers who travel to Kafiristan to establish themselves as kings. \n\nExperience Kipling's captivating narrative in a unique, book-like format on your DS. Adjust text size, customize background music, and use the bookmark feature to track your progress. The game’s search function allows you to easily locate this and other classic works by author, genre, or length. Discover insightful introductions and author biographies to enrich your reading experience. \n\nHold your DS like a traditional book and navigate the pages with the touch screen. While the DS screen presented some challenges for early e-readers, this collection offers a portable and accessible way to delve into a timeless story of ambition, deception, and the perils of empire."
    },
